Dear ian Smith,

Thank you for your submission to UIST 2026! We will soon begin setting up t=
he reviewing system. As you may have noticed in the submission form, when y=
ou submit to UIST you are also asked to provide reviews to the community: e=
ach paper will receive reviews from 2 external experts as well as 2 Associa=
te Chairs from our Program Committee. We therefore expect that between the =
authors of one paper, 4 reviews will be provided to other UIST papers.

So that we can get sufficient expert reviewers, please volunteer on PCS to =
review for UIST. You can do so here: https://new.precisionconference.com/re=
view_volunteering . To ensure that you are matched to submissions appropria=
te to your expertise, you can upload sample publications here: https://new.=
precisionconference.com/sample_pubs .

We are cc=E2=80=99ing all co-authors on this email. You are welcome to dist=
ribute reviewing responsibility as is appropriate to your seniorities.

We also note that there is one more deadline coming: April 9th EOD AOE is t=
he deadline for the mandatory alt text for all figures and tables in your p=
aper. It is also the deadline for the optional video figure and supplementa=
ry materials.

Thank you again! We look forward to looking through the submissions.

Amy Pavel, Anhong Guo, Clemens Klokmose, Jean Song, Juho Kim, and Valkyrie =
Savage

