seven day social media detox.  Not sure if it was Ash or Tom who once said
they had to get off facebook for their mental health, but I definitely
understand it.  I have to say that being as offline as much as possible is
at first quite disorienting but then astonishingly liberating. This was
necessitated when my hand-written record of the =E2=80=9Cnumber of pages re=
ad
today=E2=80=9D was diminishing while average daily screen time (reported by=
