Email from DeKalb County Tax Commissioner's Office Explore the Achievements=
 of Your Tax Commissioner's Office DeKalb County Tax Commissioner's Office =
releases its 2025 Annual Report Tax Commissioner Nicole M. Golden is encour=
aging taxpayers to review the office's 2025 Annual Report. The report detai=
ls the important work done by the tax commissioner=E2=80=99s office in coll=
ecting and disbursing nearly $2 billion in revenue for county services. =E2=
=80=9CI am proud to share the achievements and fiscal responsibility this o=
ffice consistently shows in motor vehicle and property tax collections,=E2=
=80=9D said Tax Commissioner Nicole Golden. =E2=80=9CIt is important for th=
e residents of DeKalb to understand the office=E2=80=99s commitment to deli=
vering excellent customer service, responsibly collecting and distributing =
revenue, and serving our community by creating informed and satisfied taxpa=
yers.=E2=80=9D   The report includes performance highlights within the prop=
erty tax and motor vehicle divisions of the tax commissioner=E2=80=99s offi=
ce, financial highlights, community outreach efforts, and customer service =
results.   =E2=80=9CWe as taxpayers must understand the importance of count=
y services and the impact it has on our daily lives. I encourage you to als=
o reflect on the county=E2=80=99s progress and services to residents.=E2=80=
=9D   The DeKalb County Tax Commissioner=E2=80=99s Office 2025 Annual Repor=
t is available online at DeKalbTax.org under the =E2=80=9CAbout=E2=80=9D me=
nu option. READ THE REPORT =E2=80=8A =E2=80=8A Invite us to your next event=
! Representatives from the DeKalb County Tax Commissioner=E2=80=99s Office =
are available to speak to community groups and help homeowners understand e=
xemptions and property taxes before the April 1 deadline to file online. Si=
nce 2016, the Tax Commissioner=E2=80=99s Office has conducted in-person and=
 online community presentations to help taxpayers understand homestead exem=
ptions and their property tax bills. Presentations are delivered to groups =
such as real estate professionals, homeowner associations and senior center=
s that are interested in learning more about services at the tax office. Or=
ganizations may contact the tax commissioner=E2=80=99s office by completing=
 an online request form at DeKalbTax.org. REQUEST A SPEAKER Follow the Tax =
Commissioner's Office on Facebook, LinkedIn, X and Bluesky @dekalbtaxga.   =
    Office of DeKalb County Tax Commissioner Nicole M. Golden | 4380 Memori=
al Drive | Decatur, GA 30032 US Unsubscribe | Update Profile | Constant Con=
tact Data Notice
